{"study_accession":"PRJNA1303656","secondary_study_accession":"SRP607761","title":"Pioneer transcription factor TAL1 reshapes chromatin architecture to direct erythroid cell fate commitment [RNAseq]","description":"Pioneer transcription factors critically regulate chromatin organization and hematopoietic cell lineage commitment. During erythropoiesis, hematopoietic stem cells undergo dynamic transcriptional and chromatin remodeling to differentiate into erythrocytes. Functionally validated pioneer factors capable of orchestrating erythropoiesis through dynamic chromatin remodeling remain limited, leaving their regulatory mechanisms incompletely resolved. Here, we identify T-cell acute lymphocytic leukemia 1(TAL1) as a pioneer factor that remodels chromatin to drive transcriptional reprogramming during erythropoiesis. By recruiting SWI/SNF complex, TAL1 drives erythroid fate specification while suppressing alternative lineages through lineage-restricted chromatin compartment reorganization. As a pioneer factor, TAL1 recruits chromatin remodelers BPTF and KMT2A to establish erythroid-specific genomic architecture. These complexes collectively execute TAL1 directed differentiation programs by transcriptionally activating erythroid regulators while repressing non-erythroid determinants. Our work establishes a generalizable chromatin accessibility-directed pioneer factor screening strategy, we identify TAL1 as a master pioneer factor and resolve its mechanism in driving erythroid commitment through 3D epigenome restructuring. Overall design: Primary human CD34+ cells from cord blood were isolated from mononuclear cells (MNC) obtained by human peripheral blood lymphocyte isolation fluid and followed by positive selection using CD34+ magnetic selective beads system (Miltenyi Biotechnology, Germany) according to the manufacturer’s protocol. Then we explored the the roles of TAL1 during early stage of erythropoiesis using an in vitro 3 phases erythroid-inducing cell culture system employing CD34+ cells from core blood. Cells were transfected with lentivirus containing shTAL1 at day 2, compared with the scramble control. BZ1 was purchased from MCE and adding in cell culture at a final concentration of 1μM, WDR5-0103 was purchased from MCE and adding in cell culture at a final concentration of 0.1μM at day 2. Experiment procedure before sequencing: 2 million cells(shLuciferase and shTAL1 erythroblasts, BZ1 and WDR5-0103 treated erythroblasts) were collected and washed twice with PBS. RNA was extracted and used as cDNA input, cDNA library was prepared by Illumina Truseq DNA library kit, and sequenced on Illumina NovaSeq 6000.","pubmed":"","geo_series":"","n_samples":15,"study_labels":[],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN50535451","study_accession":"PRJNA1303656","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Erythroid cells, WDR5 rep3, Day7","description":"Erythroid cells, WDR5 rep3, Day7","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9160662","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-06-27","attributes":[["source_name","Cord blood"],["tissue","Cord blood"],["cell_type","Erythroid cells"],["treatment","WDR5"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR34930184","experiment_accession":"SRX30053737","library_layout":"PAIRED","library_selection":"cDNA","instrument_model":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000","read_count":23176081,"base_count":6952824300,"first_public":"2026-06-27","experiment_title":"Illumina NovaSeq 6000 sequencing: GSM9160662: Erythroid cells, WDR5 rep3, Day7 Homo sapiens RNA-Seq"}],"labels":[],"single_cell":false},{"sample_accession":"SAMN50535452","study_accession":"PRJNA1303656","blood_class":"cord_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"Erythroid cells, WDR5 rep2, Day7","description":"Erythroid cells, WDR5 rep2, Day7","sex":"","geo_sample":"GSM9160661","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2026-06-27","attributes":[["source_name","Cord blood"],["tissue","Cord blood"